records.prompt:
Use case: style-transfer.
Asset type: visual-direction proof for a pig desktop companion game, NOT a runtime sprite sheet.
Input images: Image 1 is the EDIT TARGET, the rejected nine-pig expression preview. Images 2 and 3 are PigHub design references for lively simplified shapes and instantly readable emotions, not collage material.
Primary request: Completely redraw the nine-expression preview into a much stronger, charming, expressive, coherent 2D character-design sheet. The rejected image looks like tiny eye and mouth decals pasted onto an inert airbrushed pig. Eliminate that problem: draw integrated, anatomically coherent faces, not pasted-on emojis. Keep ONE canonical round pink pig identity across all nine cells: same bean-shaped chubby body, large integrated face toward the left, floppy ears, tiny rounded dark hooves, short curly tail. Clean warm rose outlines with deliberate variable line weight, flat peach-pink fills, minimal carefully placed cel shading, witty elastic facial acting. Take the graphic simplicity and expressive appeal from the PigHub references, but redraw an original unified interpretation. Less generic mobile-game clipart, no shiny plastic, no muddy airbrush, no gradients covering everything.
Composition: square, exactly 3 columns by 3 rows, generous even transparent gutters, each entire pig clearly visible. Consistent three-quarter left-facing view, scale, body proportions and standing pose; slight ear/cheek acting only. Make the face sufficiently large to read at a 120-pixel desktop size. No labels, no Chinese text, no props, no backgrounds.
Nine expressions row-major:
1 default bean eyes, relaxed tiny natural smile, quietly endearing;
2 genuine delighted squint, lifted cheeks, broad curved smile with a tiny tongue, infectious goofy delight;
3 exhausted dead-fish half-lids, tiny flat mouth, deadpan comic stare clearly different from 7;
4 comically aggrieved: huge shimmering wet oval eyes, dramatically upturned inner brows, big blue tear streams and a trembling pout, adorable not distressed;
5 pupils-earthquake: tall wide eyes with tiny offset pupils, lifted eyebrows, small stunned mouth, visually bewildered but NOT horror;
6 mischievous smile: asymmetric knowing squint, one raised eyebrow and an unmistakable smug cheeky side grin;
7 speechless judgment: sideways narrowed gaze, lowered flat eyebrows, compressed unimpressed mouth;
8 sleepy: heavy drooping lids, limp ears, soft small yawn, no extra face or symbols;
9 jaw-dropped surprise: large rounded shocked eyes and an integrated open rounded jaw with dark mouth interior and small pink tongue, no teeth, no dislocated mouth.
Crucial facial anatomy: two eyes only, one snout with exactly two nostrils only, one mouth only; mouth belongs on the lower FACE immediately beside/below the snout, never floating halfway across the body or on belly. All facial marks match the head perspective and line weight. Different emotions must be visually obvious, not a sequence of nearly identical faces. Hands/limbs do not change identity. Keep all pigs fully contained and separated, no cropping, no scary anatomy, no additional pigs.
Output: a polished hand-drawn 2D expression proof with genuine alpha transparency. This is a preview for art direction, not an assertion that release assets are finished.
